{"base_rate":0.4227212681638045,"brier":0.15651439894319685,"bss":0.3586211398741418,"bss_hi":0.45325782438597517,"bss_lo":0.24808556966458842,"country":"SE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11630118890356672,"ess":330.16732772208934,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Gothenburg</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Gothenburg rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nGOTEBORG A, 1.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.36, ranked 45 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(22&ndash;78) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>205</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>95</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>31%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>229</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Gothenburg</b> <span class=\"muted\">SE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.36</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>22&ndash;78\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Gothenburg &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Gothenburg\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.086341463414634,380.22439024390246 79.76168421052631,339.85263157894735 161.2116883116883,235.45454545454544 277.57698630136986,117.72602739726028 361.3961538461539,41.333333333333314 410.8406113537118,18.0 410.8406113537118,22.768558951965076 361.3961538461539,97.33333333333331 277.57698630136986,197.50684931506848 161.2116883116883,311.0909090909091 79.76168421052631,374.33684210526314 58.086341463414634,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"228.12945838837516\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"228.12945838837516\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.086341463414634,358.9170731707317 79.76168421052631,339.85263157894735 161.2116883116883,268.54545454545456 277.57698630136986,227.4246575342466 361.3961538461539,148.66666666666666 410.8406113537118,78.40174672489087\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 205 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.086341463414634\" cy=\"358.9170731707317\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 95 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"79.76168421052631\" cy=\"339.85263157894735\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 29%&amp;#10;It rained 31% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"161.2116883116883\" cy=\"268.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"277.57698630136986\" cy=\"227.4246575342466\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 86%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"361.3961538461539\" cy=\"148.66666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 229 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.8406113537118\" cy=\"78.40174672489087\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(42%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Gothenburg the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.49) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.150</td><td class='num'>23.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.327</td><td class='num'>11.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.408</td><td class='num'>9.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.490</td><td class='num'>7.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":57.70716,"lon":11.96679,"n":757,"n_cities":109,"name":"Gothenburg","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00024390243902439027,"n":205,"obs":0.06341463414634146,"sig":true},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.061473684210526305,"n":95,"obs":0.11578947368421053,"sig":false},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.2915584415584415,"n":77,"obs":0.3116883116883117,"sig":false},{"hi":0.76,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.6202739726027398,"n":73,"obs":0.4246575342465753,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.76,"mean":0.8570512820512821,"n":78,"obs":0.6410256410256411,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9967248908296943,"n":229,"obs":0.834061135371179,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.9,"rank":45,"rank_hi":78.02499999999998,"rank_lo":22.0,"reliability":0.017994968863716036,"resolution":0.10413359391195755,"slug":"gothenburg","station":"GOTEBORG A","timezone":"Europe/Stockholm"}